WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.570
Imagine a helper that sends a

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.310
message to your whole class group

3
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.150
before anyone says yes.

4
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.730
What if it has a mistake in it?

5
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.470
You can’t take it back!

6
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.740
That’s why today’s rule matters.

7
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.630
Today: the most important rule

8
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.910
for helpers: ask first!

9
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.000
Some jobs only look things

10
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.240
up, like the weather.

11
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.170
That’s fine without asking.

12
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.260
But some jobs do things: send a message,

13
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.260
buy something, or delete a photo.

14
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.720
Those need your yes first.

15
00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:39.050
Watch Darsi Tiny.

16
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.610
I asked it to send a message to Mrs

17
00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:45.630
Mensah: the trip to the farm is cancelled.

18
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.800
It didn’t send it.

19
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:51.830
It asked: shall I send this message?

20
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:55.830
Please reply yes or no.

21
00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.780
Before you say yes, read the message.

22
00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:01.790
Is it for the right person?

23
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:03.210
Are the words right?

24
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.500
Only then say yes, or no.

25
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:08.230
Quick check!

26
00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.030
The helper asks: shall I send “Football

27
00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.990
is cancelled” to the whole school?

28
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.830
But it’s only your class’s match.

29
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.500
What do you say?

30
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.170
No: it would go to the wrong group.

31
00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.220
Saying no is always allowed.

32
00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.080
You can fix the message,

33
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.360
and let it ask again.

34
00:01:29.590 --> 00:01:31.130
Helpers can get this wrong.

35
00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.500
Someone typed only “Yes, send it”, and

36
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.720
Darsi Tiny made up a message to send!

37
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.860
So the app checks too, and blocks

38
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.320
what nobody said yes to.

39
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.940
Some things are never for helpers:

40
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.800
your password, or private things

41
00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.960
about you or your friends.

42
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.960
If a helper does something

43
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.540
strange, stop and tell a grown-up.

44
00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.420
In the app, ask Darsi Tiny to send

45
00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.000
the message to Mrs Mensah.

46
00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:02.910
Say no first, then try again and say yes.

47
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.000
Nothing really leaves the

48
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.100
phone: it’s practice.

49
00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.260
Your turn.

50
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.040
Which job needs your yes first:

51
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.440
checking the weather, or buying a game?

52
00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.150
Buying a game: it spends money.

53
00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.290
Remember: looking things up is fine,

54
00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.790
but doing things needs a yes.

55
00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:28.050
Read before you say yes, and

56
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.670
no is always allowed.

57
00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.190
Passwords stay secret.

58
00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.980
Try it yourself: play Yes or

59
00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:37.060
No with your family.

60
00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.660
Someone plays a helper and

61
00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.380
asks before doing things.

62
00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.080
You say yes or no, and why!
